{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Parent\n\nEpic `77e3-28e2-31ec-47ec`, authorized at full scope by the operator on 2026-11-02.\nDeliverable 2. Depends on `fe94-2e22-ea9e-46f7`, which establishes the net-mechanism\ncriterion this story's own change must satisfy.\n\n## The gap\n\nA mechanism admitted by a `# mechanism-ok:` marker is admitted FOREVER. Measured at\n`origin/main` `346a76f1c87`:\n\n- The grammar is `scripts/_mechanism_delta/markers.py:20` (`_MARKER_RE`), separators at\n  `:23` — `(\"—\", \"--\", \"-\", \":\")` — capture at `:42-43`. Three fields: kind, name, reason.\n  It is ONE LINE: `parse_marker` (`:37-44`) reads a single line, `_record` (`:66-68`)\n  stores that line's reason, so continuation lines are invisible to the ratchet.\n- `compare.py:89` partitions `counters.new` against the harvested markers, `:91-92`\n  emitting the `admitted` line, so a nonblank reason admits the key. A blank reason becomes\n  an error in `_blank_marker_errors` (`:58`, called at `:87`) reaching the exit at `:99`.\n- Nothing parses a ticket id out of the reason, nor checks that a referenced ticket\n  exists, is open, or ever closes.\n\nSo `# mechanism-ok: env_var REBAR_X — remove after the migration` blesses the mechanism\npermanently: the migration closes, the marker stays, the ratchet never looks again. The\nadmission is a one-way door with no expiry.\n\n## The convention exists but is not enforced\n\nEvery tracked file was parsed with the ratchet's own `parse_marker`, excluding the\ngrammar's 6 definition sites (`markers.py`, `compare.py`, `check_mechanism_delta.py`,\n`test_mechanism_delta.py`, `docs/architecture.md`, `AGENTS.md`):\n\n- **90 real admission markers.** 3 further hits quote the grammar rather than admit\n  anything, so are excluded: `Makefile:289`, ADR `0112:232`,\n  `src/rebar/_config_resolvers.py:213`.\n- **75 already name a two- or four-quad id**, e.g. `1e24-bfc0` on the Gerrit-retry\n  `ci_gate` markers in `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml`.\n- **1 names an ALIAS only**: `src/rebar/reconciler/_ref_lock.py:78` cites\n  `metaphoric-late-creature`. An alias IS resolvable, AGENTS.md making it the preferred\n  write form, so the narrowed grammar must accept aliases or this marker breaks wrongly.\n- **14 name no resolvable id** — mostly a **deprecated 4-digit quad** (`c6ce`, `aa9e`,\n  `adab`, `5169`, `1cef`, `48bd`, `85a5`) or a Jira id (`REB-640`), with\n  `src/rebar/llm/config_readers.py:257` naming nothing. `tests/_child_hooks.py:1` DOES name\n  `b939-bc68-1cb2-4ee9`, but on line 3, which the single-line grammar never reads; moving\n  the id onto the marker line migrates it.\n\nAGENTS.md deprecates the bare 4-digit quad because \"in a store of any size those quads\ncollide, so they resolve to nothing.\" Those markers already cite an unresolvable ticket —\na sunset reference that means nothing, with nothing to detect it.\n\nThe baseline carries **647 mechanisms** (`.github/mechanism-baseline.json`), so the 90\nadmitted sit against ~557 grandfathered; this story governs the admitted set.\n\nA marker-admitted new mechanism DOES land today: at `346a76f1c87`, `--check` reports\n`active=647 new=32 increased=0 stale=0`, exit 0. Bug `a1f1-a30d-2d50-4f5a`, which once\nmade a new mechanism unlandable, is closed, though the docstring at\n`src/rebar/_config_resolvers.py:210-215` still claims otherwise. Half 2's precheck can\ntherefore be admitted by its own marker, so the ACs below are stated as exit codes rather\nthan as `new == 0`, which is not a reachable state.\n\n## The change\n\nTwo halves.\n\n**Half 1 — the marker names a sunset ticket.** Narrow the admission grammar so the third\nfield opens with a resolvable rebar ticket id rather than arbitrary prose. A marker whose\nid does not resolve is no admission; the ratchet fails as it would for a blank reason.\n\"Resolvable\" is a SHAPE check, not a store lookup: the grammar matches the alias,\ntwo-quad, and four-quad forms the resolver accepts, and never opens the store.\n`scripts/_mechanism_delta/` does no ticket resolution today, and `make lint` runs where the\n`tickets` ref need not be fetched, so a lookup would add the dependency this story states\nit avoids. A bare 4-digit quad is deprecated, so is not matched. A well-formed id naming\nno existing ticket passes Half 1; Half 2 is what gives the id meaning. The id must sit on\nthe marker line, since the grammar reads one line.\n\n**Half 2 — that ticket cannot close while the marker remains.** Add a deterministic\nprecheck to the completion-verification close path: when the ticket being closed is named\nas the sunset ticket of a `# mechanism-ok:` marker still in the tree, the close is refused,\nthe refusal naming the marker's file plus line. Both ids are canonicalized before\ncomparison — the marker's and the one the close is invoked with — or the alias at\n`_ref_lock.py:78` would never block its own close.\n\n## What this retires\n\nRequired by `fe94`'s net-mechanism criterion; this is the first change judged by it.\n\nThis ADDS one deterministic close precheck and RETIRES the free-text reason as an\nadmission: afterwards only a resolvable ticket id admits a mechanism, so the \"write any\nsentence and pass\" path at `compare.py:89-92` ceases to exist.\n\n## Where the close refusal goes\n\nThe close gate has NO pluggable deterministic check — measured, not assumed: no\n`_PRECHECKS` tuple and no precheck registry in `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py`.\nPlan review has `det_invariants.run_project_det_checks` driven by `exec: \"DET\"` overlay\nentries; the close path has no equivalent.\n\nThe seam is the straight-line sequence in `_completion_precheck` (`:604`), whose refusals\nrun BEFORE the LLM verifier at `:694`. The landing check `_check_work_landed` (`:151`) is\ncalled at `:685`, raising at `:215-222`; a new refusal is one more call there. Precedent\nfor reading state beyond git history: `_check_file_impact_vs_diff` (`:289`) reads landed\ncommits' diffs. The sunset scan reads tracked file contents — wider than any existing\nprecheck, stated not inferred.\n\n## The --force caveat, stated rather than hidden\n\n`_gate_skip_expectation` (`:554`, called at `:636`) short-circuits the ENTIRE precheck\nblock under `--force=\"<reason>\"`, so no refusal in this gate is unconditional and the ACs\nsay \"absent a human override\". Per AGENTS.md agents must not use `--force`.\n\n## Portability\n\nHalf 2 runs in-process in the close path, so it fires in any environment that can close a\nticket. Half 1 runs inside `scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py`, whose trigger is the `make\nlint` target rather than a CI provider, so it fires with no CI present. Both halves are\ndeterministic — neither calls an LLM, so no provider or model dependency arises.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Grammar, one test per case: `scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits\n      non-zero for a new mechanism whose marker reason does not open with a resolvable\n      ticket id; non-zero for a bare 4-digit single-quad; zero for an alias; zero for a\n      two- or four-quad id.\n- [ ] Close precheck, one test per case: closing a ticket named as the sunset ticket of a\n      marker still present in the tree is refused absent a human `--force` override, with\n      the error naming the marker's file plus line; closing that ticket succeeds once the\n      marker is removed; closing a ticket named by no marker is unaffected.\n- [ ] Two invariants, one test each: removing a mechanism still passes the ratchet,\n      guarding the shrink-only asymmetry at `compare.py:99` where `counters.stale` is\n      never consulted; the new precheck fires with no CI environment configured.\n- [ ] All 14 real-site markers that do not name a resolvable id are migrated to one, with\n      the remaining 76 (75 id + 1 alias) parsing under the narrowed grammar. Verified by\n      `make verify`.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes.\n\n## Measurement base\n\nEvery citation and count above was read from `origin/main` at `346a76f1c87`, where the\nratchet was also run. The 90/75/1/14 split was measured by parsing every site with\n`parse_marker`, not sampled."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793695363324949001,"uuid":"2314bedd-1d3d-48e3-8ab4-4f1a7c79acaf"}